    {
      "type": "view",
      "title": "Bind, author, collect, emit",
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "slideFrame",
          "body": [
            {
              "type": "slideHeading",
              "title": "Styles move through four steps: bind, author, collect, emit",
              "lede": "Collection is a side effect of rendering, so the CSS that ships matches the HTML that rendered."
            },
            {
              "type": "slidePipeline",
              "start": "theme",
              "end": "CSS",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "title": "Bind",
                  "body": "`createDistillery` fixes the prefix, tokens, and scope selector. No brand of its own."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Author",
                  "body": "`createStyleModule` records typed declarations once, at module load."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Collect",
                  "body": "Resolving a class name during render pulls in that handle."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Emit",
                  "body": "`renderStyles` writes a readable sheet or a compact payload."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "logo": false,
          "tone": "page",
          "footer": {
            "brand": "Distillate",
            "section": "How it works",
            "sectionNumber": "02",
            "url": "https://elastic.github.io/distillate"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "view",
      "title": "Tokens are typed paths",
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "slideFrame",
          "body": [
            {
              "type": "slideHeading",
              "title": "Tokens are **typed paths**, not strings",
              "lede": "Interpolating a token records a dependency. `lightDark` folds into `light-dark()`, `cq` inlines with no custom property, and unread tokens are pruned."
            },
            {
              "type": "slideCodeTrace",
              "panels": [
                {
                  "file": "distillery.ts",
                  "language": "ts",
                  "text": "const distillery = createDistillery({\n  prefix: 'eui',\n  themeScope: '.eui-view',\n  theme: {\n    colors: {\n      ink: lightDark('#111', '#eee'),\n    },\n    gap: cq('8px', '2cqi'),\n  },\n});",
                  "lineNumbers": {
                    "highlight": "6, 8"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "file": "demo.ts",
                  "language": "ts",
                  "text": "const demo =\n  distillery.createStyleModule(\n    'demo',\n    ({ css, tokens }) => ({\n      root: css`\n        color: ${tokens.colors.ink};\n        padding: ${tokens.gap};\n      `,\n    })\n  );",
                  "lineNumbers": {
                    "highlight": "6-7"
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "logo": false,
          "tone": "page",
          "footer": {
            "brand": "Distillate",
            "section": "How it works",
            "sectionNumber": "02",
            "url": "https://elastic.github.io/distillate"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "view",
      "title": "A module returns handles",
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "slideFrame",
          "body": [
            {
              "type": "slideHeading",
              "title": "A module returns **handles**, not class names",
              "lede": "The same handle emits `.callout-root` or `.a`, depending on the resolver."
            },
            {
              "type": "slideCode",
              "file": "callout.ts — adapted from docs/concepts/authoring.md",
              "language": "ts",
              "text": "const callout = distillery.createStyleModule('callout', ({ css, decls, tokens }) => ({\n  root: css`\n    color: ${tokens.colors.ink};\n    &:hover { color: ${tokens.colors.accent}; }\n    @media (min-width: 600px) { padding: 16px; }\n  `,\n  title: css`font-weight: 600;`,\n  tone: variants(['calm', 'loud'] as const, (tone) => css`\n    outline-color: ${tone === 'calm' ? tokens.colors.surface : tokens.colors.accent};\n  `),\n  hoverTitle: rule(\n    (h) => `${h.root}:hover ${h.title}`,\n    decls`color: ${tokens.colors.accent};`\n  ),\n}));",
              "lineNumbers": {
                "highlight": "4-5, 8, 11"
              }
            }
          ],
          "logo": false,
          "tone": "page",
          "footer": {
            "brand": "Distillate",
            "section": "How it works",
            "sectionNumber": "02",
            "url": "https://elastic.github.io/distillate"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "view",
      "title": "The render decides what ships",
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "slideFrame",
          "body": [
            {
              "type": "slideHeading",
              "title": "The render decides what ships",
              "lede": "Resolving a class name collects it. Everything the render never reached is pruned from an artifact."
            },
            {
              "type": "slideList",
              "items": [
                {
                  "term": "use(module)",
                  "body": "Every non-variant entry on the module."
                },
                {
                  "term": "useHandles",
                  "body": "Those handles, plus any `rule` or `media` whose selector deps are **all** live."
                },
                {
                  "term": "variants",
                  "body": "Ship only when a render names one, such as `tone.loud`."
                },
                {
                  "term": "theme tokens",
                  "body": "Only the paths a collected declaration reads, or `useThemeVar`."
                },
                {
                  "term": "vars defaults",
                  "body": "Only the keys each handle actually reads."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "logo": false,
          "tone": "page",
          "footer": {
            "brand": "Distillate",
            "section": "How it works",
